        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{3}^{21}\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}{log}_{7}(\\frac{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}{3})\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\log_{7}\\left(\\frac{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}{3}\\right).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x \\ln{\\left(7 \\right)}}\\,\u27f9\\,\\ln{\\left(7 \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $21$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{3}^{21}\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}{log}_{7}(\\frac{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{3}^{21}{log}_{7}(\\frac{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{0}^{1}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}7\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(7 \\right)}}{5}\\int_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\operatorname{ln}7\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}\\right)|_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}7}{2}\\cdot (1-0)\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}7}{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
